## Stock check before transfer

- Orris Liquid is the user's **9% w/w supplied-product stock in DEP**, not the old 30% preparation and not 9% pure irones.
- Alpha Irone is **10% w/w in DEP**.
- Ambrettolide is **10% w/w in DPG**; Tonkarome is **20% w/w in TEC**. Existing user records confirm those preparations. Do not prepare or dilute them again.
- The methyl-ionone row refers to the **existing Alpha Isomethyl Ionone / AIMI bottle** reconciled in INV-USER-20260904-003, not a new or substituted methyl-ionone grade.
- Vetiver means the owned **Indian Vetiver EO, volume grade**, not Haiti vetiver or another replacement.
- Cashmeran is neat; Osmanthus is the premium 10% DPG stock; E2MB is the existing 0.1% DPG working stock.
- The c4d5 gate has not incorporated four existing identity/preparation corrections. This card records physical label intent; it does not silently repair runtime authority. Confirm sufficient stock remains and that each prepared stock is homogeneous and pipetteable.

## Pour sequence

Finish each basket before moving to the next. Within each basket the raw transfer only decreases; equal amounts use ingredient-name order. Carrier already present in a stock is **not poured again**.

Basket key: **1** always used; **2** vetivers; **3** woods; **6** musks; **7** muguet/lavender; **9** ylang/orange flower/narcotics; **11** iris/orris; **12** edible smells; **15** fruits.

